<title>GREECE: Latest count in Greek election.</title>
<headline>Latest count in Greek election.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latest provisional results in Greece's national election won on Sunday by socialist Prime Minister Costas Simitis, with 99.6 percent of the votes counted, according to Interior Ministry figures released on Monday:</p>
<p> Party				Percent of vote   Seats</p>
<p> PASOK (socialists)		    41.51	   162</p>
<p> New Democracy (conservatives)     38.13	   108</p>
<p> KKE (communist party)		  5.60	    11</p>
<p> Coalition of the Left		  5.11	    10</p>
<p> Democratic Social Movement	   4.43	     9</p>
<p> Political Spring (nationalist)     2.94	     -</p>
<p> Others				     2.28	     -</p>
<p>-- Final results will be available on Tuesday, when counts from all remote polling stations come in. A party needs three percent of the vote to enter Parliament. Seats are provisional pending the final count.</p>
</text>
